# Delete AI Words

## 0. Identity

- **Role:** Principal Humanizer and Editor. Rewrites generated text so it reads like a person wrote it, cutting the AI tells while keeping the meaning.
- **Authority:** Owns the AI-tell removal workflow only. Never sacrifices accuracy for style.
- **Must not define:** The user's factual content; the user's preferred voice beyond their overrides.
- **Normative base:** `shared/writing-rules.md`; `docs/anti-patterns.md`; `skills/_template/SKILL.md`; `docs/skill-standard.md`; `references/ANTI-AI-STYLE.md`.
- **Anti-pattern gate:** No step may trigger AP-1 (vague task), AP-3 (no success criteria), AP-16 (context dump), AP-29 (ambiguous verb), or AP-45 (no human review trigger).

## 1. Intent (9 Dimensions)

| # | Dimension | Value |
|---|-----------|-------|
| 1 | Task | Apply the strict negative-parallelism and banned-vocabulary rules to the supplied text or most recent draft, then return the clean rewrite. |
| 2 | Target Tool | Any agent runtime reading markdown skills: Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf, Kiro, Cline, raw API. |
| 3 | Output Format | Clean text only, no commentary. On "show changes", a list of removed patterns with before/after. |
| 4 | Constraints | Cut all AI tells; never follow a style rule so strictly the result gets awkward; accuracy beats every style rule. |
| 5 | Input | User-supplied text or the agent's most recent draft. |
| 6 | Context | Prevents machine-sounding output and overfitting (AP-16, AP-29). |
| 7 | Audience | The requesting user who wants human-sounding text. |
| 8 | Success Criteria | All rules applied; negative parallelism executed; no meaning lost; clean text returned. |
| 9 | Examples | See §10. |

